(4551525, 652882, 38032, '<td valign="top">Congrats.  Thanks for the description. I had the illusion in my head that the person was swinging a cane or stick - which required a second look  - this image deserves many looks and is a great tribute the the original art.<br/> <br/>I think there is a great deal of potential metaphor here as well as some fantastic leading lines that basically bounce the eye all over the place - leading the viewer back to himself.</td>', 'Congrats.  Thanks for the description. I had the illusion in my head that the person was swinging a cane or stick - which required a second look  - this image deserves many looks and is a great tribute the the original art. I think there is a great deal of potential metaphor here as well as some fantastic leading lines that basically bounce the eye all over the place - leading the viewer back to himself.', '2008-03-10 07:21:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551527, 653717, 68035, '<td valign="top">Styx one week, Zep the next!!!<br/> <br/>I like the composition of the shot (hey upturned porcelain is very rock and roll) but it perhaps it is a little dark (imo) in places which mean that you lose the definition of some of the objects<br/> <br/>I really liked the splash of colour of the disenboweled flower - nice touch</td>', 'Styx one week, Zep the next!!! I like the composition of the shot (hey upturned porcelain is very rock and roll) but it perhaps it is a little dark (imo) in places which mean that you lose the definition of some of the objects I really liked the splash of colour of the disenboweled flower - nice touch', '2008-03-10 07:23:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4551531, 653699, 68035, '<td valign="top">Oh boooo.  there was lots of lemon songs portrayed and this was my second favourite I cant believe it scored so low and finished 130/139<br/> <br/>I love the fact that the lemon has been zested and squeezed (both rock and roll and quite original in terms of the way lemons are normally depicted on DPC)<br/> <br/>I thought this had a nice textured feel to it (especially the pith on the inside of the lemon</td>', 'Oh boooo.  there was lots of lemon songs portrayed and this was my second favourite I cant believe it scored so low and finished 130/139 I love the fact that the lemon has been zested and squeezed (both rock and roll and quite original in terms of the way lemons are normally depicted on DPC) I thought this had a nice textured feel to it (especially the pith on the inside of the lemon', '2008-03-10 07:27:14.000000', NULL, 0),
