(4553349, 652882, 20941, '<td valign="top">You Rock Like Zeppelin Steve! Congrats on the Ribbon and PB! You planned and executed this beautifully! WTG</td>', 'You Rock Like Zeppelin Steve! Congrats on the Ribbon and PB! You planned and executed this beautifully! WTG', '2008-03-10 20:42:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553354, 653729, 20941, '<td valign="top">Fantastic interpretation and awsome b/w! Congrats on the Ribbon!!</td>', 'Fantastic interpretation and awsome b/w! Congrats on the Ribbon!!', '2008-03-10 20:44:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553358, 652599, 66384, '<td valign="top">Susan, I REALLY like this shot. I like the grain, the crop, the model and pose, the costume (even the flashlight mic). I like the pastel highlights that look like stage lights. Your hair looks fabulous. I like the power and energy. You went all out, and I am very impressed. Wow!!</td>', 'Susan, I REALLY like this shot. I like the grain, the crop, the model and pose, the costume (even the flashlight mic). I like the pastel highlights that look like stage lights. Your hair looks fabulous. I like the power and energy. You went all out, and I am very impressed. Wow!!', '2008-03-10 20:47:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553377, 653683, 66384, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot, Kelli. Really nice processing for your purpose. It looks like a painted illustration. Nice setup: model, pose, costume, back drop.</td>', 'I like this a lot, Kelli. Really nice processing for your purpose. It looks like a painted illustration. Nice setup: model, pose, costume, back drop.', '2008-03-10 20:56:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553382, 652599, 62787, '<td valign="top">Very cool! :) Great pose, cool composition, and the processing really appeals to me. A worthy Led Zep tribute! :)</td>', 'Very cool! :) Great pose, cool composition, and the processing really appeals to me. A worthy Led Zep tribute! :)', '2008-03-10 20:59:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553424, 653567, 35334, '<td valign="top">Jamie,<br/> <br/>I''m posting a comment because you asked for comments in the thread Deb started. I''m afraid I can''t help much. I''m not a Led Zeppelin fan so I didn''t vote on this challenge and I haven''t even looked through the winners. I don''t know any of the lyrics so all the titles just go whizzing past me.<br/> <br/>So I''m looking at this just as a picture without reference to the music. It''s obviously humorous; I was ROFLMAO! It shows a guy who is definitely in the wrong place or at the wrong time, yet he is pressing on, seemingly oblivious to the snow. But his expression shows that it is getting to him.<br/> <br/>It is technically good. I like the backlighting. It is nice that you have the dark background of the bushes so that his hair stands out.<br/> <br/>--DanW</td>', 'Jamie, I''m posting a comment because you asked for comments in the thread Deb started. I''m afraid I can''t help much. I''m not a Led Zeppelin fan so I didn''t vote on this challenge and I haven''t even looked through the winners. I don''t know any of the lyrics so all the titles just go whizzing past me. So I''m looking at this just as a picture without reference to the music. It''s obviously humorous; I was ROFLMAO! It shows a guy who is definitely in the wrong place or at the wrong time, yet he is pressing on, seemingly oblivious to the snow. But his expression shows that it is getting to him. It is technically good. I like the backlighting. It is nice that you have the dark background of the bushes so that his hair stands out. --DanW', '2008-03-10 21:21:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553467, 653582, 79720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by david_c:</b></div><hr/><i> Great composition. Should be top 20. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>OK...top 1, anyway. Congrats on a great find.</td>', 'Originally posted by david_c: Great composition. Should be top 20.  OK...top 1, anyway. Congrats on a great find.', '2008-03-10 21:38:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553469, 652882, 79720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by david_c:</b></div><hr/><i> No, no, no. This is the cover of "Physical Graffiti". What are you, a Britney Spears fan? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>ahhh, I realize now the challenge was "song titles or lyrics", not album covers. Houses of the Holy does indeed appear on the PG album. :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by david_c: No, no, no. This is the cover of "Physical Graffiti". What are you, a Britney Spears fan?  ahhh, I realize now the challenge was "song titles or lyrics", not album covers. Houses of the Holy does indeed appear on the PG album. :-)', '2008-03-10 21:41:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553564, 653791, 70514, '<td valign="top">The texture the rocks against the water droplets really make this for me.  And the beautiful sky doesn''t hurt either, of course.</td>', 'The texture the rocks against the water droplets really make this for me.  And the beautiful sky doesn''t hurt either, of course.', '2008-03-10 22:18:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4553741, 653450, 9668, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous image. Really stood out to me. Very cool to see this familiar rocks in a different and foggy way (I thought this was Indian Beach until I read your comments). Nice composition.</td>', 'Gorgeous image. Really stood out to me. Very cool to see this familiar rocks in a different and foggy way (I thought this was Indian Beach until I read your comments). Nice composition.', '2008-03-10 23:15:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554046, 653810, 53814, '<td valign="top">Beautiful work, you should put this in the poetry side challenge.</td>', 'Beautiful work, you should put this in the poetry side challenge.', '2008-03-11 01:01:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554047, 653729, 41337, '<td valign="top">Congrats Enzo! Wonderful image.</td>', 'Congrats Enzo! Wonderful image.', '2008-03-11 01:02:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554062, 653567, 30982, '<td valign="top">I thought this was hilarious - I seriously got a kick out of it.  In looking at it again, I''ve got to say that it''s also well done in my opinion.  Very good exposure, color, for shooting against snow.  Good choice of lowish light to use to give you that.  Well composed, too.  I''m kind of at a loss as to how to tell you to get this score above a 6.  It should have.  I think my little experiment with the thread you posted this to is simply telling me that there sometimes is no real reason a shot doesn''t score as well as it should.  This meets the challenge, has humor, is technically pretty good.  Perhaps someone with more technial expertise can help you along those lines.  And tell your hubby he is a great sport!</td>', 'I thought this was hilarious - I seriously got a kick out of it.  In looking at it again, I''ve got to say that it''s also well done in my opinion.  Very good exposure, color, for shooting against snow.  Good choice of lowish light to use to give you that.  Well composed, too.  I''m kind of at a loss as to how to tell you to get this score above a 6.  It should have.  I think my little experiment with the thread you posted this to is simply telling me that there sometimes is no real reason a shot doesn''t score as well as it should.  This meets the challenge, has humor, is technically pretty good.  Perhaps someone with more technial expertise can help you along those lines.  And tell your hubby he is a great sport!', '2008-03-11 01:15:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554183, 653603, 90394, '<td valign="top">An ordinary capture, with some technicals that are distracting - such as the noisy building in the background. Could have popped more if it were darker, and a bit sharper. Some over exposure on the teacup distracts me somewhat. Fits the challenge theme in mediocre fashion, but doesn''t say "Led Zepplin" to me. I''d give this a 5.</td>', 'An ordinary capture, with some technicals that are distracting - such as the noisy building in the background. Could have popped more if it were darker, and a bit sharper. Some over exposure on the teacup distracts me somewhat. Fits the challenge theme in mediocre fashion, but doesn''t say "Led Zepplin" to me. I''d give this a 5.', '2008-03-11 03:08:46.000000', NULL, 0),
