(4582002, 653342, 84452, '<td valign="top">I love the southwest Michigan lighthouses and have taken hundreds of the St. Joe light myself. I''ve always wanted to get a classic ice-covered lighthouse image, but now that I live in Florida, that simply isn''t going to happen. I''ve learned that you pretty much have to be there on the day that "it" happens. While I still have a home in Berrien County, but I opt for the warmer weather during those cold, icy days on Lake Michigan. Drat!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-23 22:48:45.</i></td>', 'I love the southwest Michigan lighthouses and have taken hundreds of the St. Joe light myself. I''ve always wanted to get a classic ice-covered lighthouse image, but now that I live in Florida, that simply isn''t going to happen. I''ve learned that you pretty much have to be there on the day that "it" happens. While I still have a home in Berrien County, but I opt for the warmer weather during those cold, icy days on Lake Michigan. Drat!', '2008-03-23 22:47:57.000000', '2008-03-23 22:48:45.000000', 0),
(4582638, 651155, 30982, '<td valign="top">I can very much see the need to have that single tree included.  It adds significantly to the balance and mood of the shot.  Excellent processing to capture the softness and stillness of the morning fog.  And yes, if this is what happens, you should definitely get up early once in awhile.</td>', 'I can very much see the need to have that single tree included.  It adds significantly to the balance and mood of the shot.  Excellent processing to capture the softness and stillness of the morning fog.  And yes, if this is what happens, you should definitely get up early once in awhile.', '2008-03-24 06:16:32.000000', NULL, 0),
